sam: FYI I opened a docs PR to consolidate 429/timeouts troubleshooting into one page and update SDK examples — need reviews + verify links. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/948
kevin: Nice. Can you add the Python SDK snippet to show backoff + context trimming? Current sample only shows node.
sam: Yes — planning to add both. Draft for py snippet: ```python
from redwood import Client
import time
client = Client()
try:
    resp = client.generate('summarize this', timeout=10)
except TooManyRequests:
    # exponential backoff
    time.sleep(2)
``` Need exact import names — @marie any naming changes in SDK 0.7?
marie: Heads up: SDK 0.7 renamed exceptions — use TooManyRequestsError and GenerateTimeoutError. Also we prefer RedwoodClient as the class name in docs. Quick corrected snippet: ```python
from redwood import RedwoodClient, TooManyRequestsError
import time
client = RedwoodClient()
for attempt in range(3):
    try:
        out = client.generate('short summary', timeout=8)
        break
    except TooManyRequestsError:
        time.sleep(2**attempt)
```
kevin: perfect. Also we should add a note about trimming context on the client vs server side and link to the context-limits page. I found a broken anchor at /docs/context#limits in the current doc, so the crossref needs fixing.
sam: Good catch. I updated the link in the PR to /docs/guides/context-limits#trimming and added a short blurb about client-side prefix trimming + server-side KV cache behavior. Can someone run quick grammar pass? small wording change in the 'fallback behavior' paragraph (clarify when we fall back to a cheaper model).
marie: I'll take grammar + run the linter locally. Also adding a short Node example for Retry-After handling. Snippet: ```js
import fetch from 'node-fetch'
async function call() {
  const res = await fetch(url, {method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(payload)})
  if (res.status === 429) {
    const retryAfter = parseInt(res.headers.get('retry-after') || '1', 10)
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, retryAfter * 1000))
    // retry logic...
  }
}
```
docs-bot: link-checker started for PR #948 — found 1 warning (context-limits anchor) — re-check after push.
kevin: Awesome. One last thing: add a tiny table of recommended backoff windows (fast-api vs high-throughput jobs). That helps SREs copy/paste.
sam: Added table + updated examples. PTAL, merging once @marie approves linter results. Thanks all :thumbsup:
